hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2761","Abu Bakr (RA) said in the narration of Jabir (RA) which I have mentioned before:\n*\Until his two feet sank into the valley's depths"," he ran until he ascended"," then he walked.\""*\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"2762","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Mu'adh: narrated to us Ayyub (meaning Ibn Waqid): narrated to us 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would run (sa'ya) in the valley of the Masil between Safa and Marwah.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"2763","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi, that 'Amr ibn Mujammi' informed them, on the authority of Musa ibn 'Uqba, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:\n\When the mount of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood still for him at Dhu al-Hulayfa during the Farewell Pilgrimage or an 'Umra"," he would say the Talbiya (Labbayk Allahumma labbayk).\""\nThen he mentioned the hadith and said:\n\""Then he came to al-Safa"," and he ran between al-Safa and al-Marwa seven times. When he passed by al-Mas'a"," he would run.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
